[TITLE]
InpWriter round-trip fixture: IRREGULAR conduit referencing a MISSING transect
TRX is never defined, so xsect_curve stays -1 while the parser's retained name
is all the writer has. Mirrors dangling_refs.inp: a strict open should reject
this model (undefined transect), the GUI's lenient open keeps it editable, and
Save must preserve the name "TRX" rather than emitting derived numerics.

[OPTIONS]
FLOW_UNITS           CFS
INFILTRATION         HORTON
FLOW_ROUTING         DYNWAVE
START_DATE           01/01/2020
START_TIME           00:00:00
END_DATE             01/02/2020
END_TIME             00:00:00
REPORT_STEP          00:15:00
ROUTING_STEP         0:00:30
MIN_SLOPE            0

[EVAPORATION]
CONSTANT   0.0
DRY_ONLY   NO

[JUNCTIONS]
;;Name  Elev  MaxDepth  InitDepth  SurDepth  Aponded
J1       10.0  8.0       0          0         0

[OUTFALLS]
;;Name  Elev  Type  StageData  Gated
O1       8.0   FREE  *          NO

[CONDUITS]
;;Name  FromNode  ToNode  Length  Roughness  InOffset  OutOffset
C1       J1        O1      400.0   0.013      0         0

[XSECTIONS]
;;Link  Shape      Geom1  Geom2  Geom3  Geom4  Barrels
C1       IRREGULAR  TRX

[REPORT]
INPUT       NO
CONTROLS    NO
NODES       ALL
LINKS       ALL

[COORDINATES]
;;Node  X-Coord  Y-Coord
J1       0.0      0.0
O1       1000.0   0.0
